Section 7 - Definitions
(57)
For the purpose of this Procedure:
arrangements: the specific terms of the activities that are proposed or implemented under one or more agreements with a partner;
agreement: a signed document between the University and a partner institution outlining agreed conditions for an activity or activities;
Contract Sponsor
: the University staff member or office responsible for implementing and managing a contract (see
Contracts Policy
);
courseware: course and subject materials, including such items as subject outlines, learning materials and teaching or assessment resources;
duly authorised signatory: the relevant delegate authorised to sign agreements under the
Contract Signing Delegations
(staff only);
Nominee: a senior member of staff nominated by a
Contract Sponsor
to fulfill the functional responsibilities associated with a third-party educational arrangement;
Responsibilities Matrix: a framework that documents agreed service costs and operational responsibilities in an educational third-party agreement.
